From ee8b947ee9f48d6c99b9e3e3166fceb2cd374136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:37:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nougat: multipoint standard rework - transactional media
 switch, strict routing/ownership, preemptive AVRCP PAUSE

Fixes the field-reported bug: with two phones connected, after the
second one preempts the first, resuming playback on the first device
stays permanently silent.

Root-cause class (audited against the standard implementations -
android11-release system/bt A2DP sink, android10-release Bluetooth app
A2dpSinkStreamHandler, BlueALSA):

- D1 race: a media-path switch was a CLEAR_TRACK + CFG_UPDATE
  two-message sequence while the BTU-thread enqueue path (delayed
  start at 5 queued frames) kept running: start_decoding could fire on
  a NULL / half-rebuilt track -> dead decode pump -> permanent silence.
- D2 routing poison: unmatched stream events fell back to slot 0; a
  stray CLOSE unbound the healthy slot 0, after which every switch
  fail-safe aborted and rx_flush stayed TRUE forever.
- D4 ownership hole: SUSPEND/STOP handlers also acted when owner==-1,
  flushing the live path of whichever peer was streaming.
- D8 policy gap: the preempted peer only got AVDTP SUSPEND; players
  that auto-reSTART then ping-ponged the shared path (switch war),
  re-opening the D1 window on every round.
- D3/D5/D7/D9: 2-slot fallback leftover in stop_with_fallback, NULL
  scb deref in the BTA media scan, accept-gate fallback feeding a
  non-owner's packets to the shared decoder, and Java disconnect/RC
  calls using the register hndl instead of the runtime streaming hndl.

Standard-aligned fixes:

- btif_media_task: new BTIF_MEDIA_AUDIO_SINK_SWITCH event +
  btif_media_task_sink_switch_req(); the switch runs as ONE media
  worker handler (stop pump, flush queue, tear down track/decoders,
  rebuild from the codec_info carried in the message), serialized with
  enqueue / rx_flush / start / stop / clear / decoder-reset through a
  recursive sink_media_lock (android11 g_mutex model).  NULL-track
  guards in start_decoding, btif_sink_write_audio and AudioTrack
  Start/WriteData (A11 parity).
- btif_av: strict stream-event routing (unmatched hndl -> drop + log,
  never slot 0); audio ownership claimed in the START router BEFORE
  the state-machine dispatch, posting the transactional switch (so the
  STARTED entry switch becomes a no-op); strict owner==ctx guards on
  all SUSPEND/STOP paths; stop_with_fallback scans all 3 slots; media
  accept gate is owner-only; OPEN-failure unbinds the pre-bound slot;
  IDLE entry clears the runtime hndl; a preempted peer additionally
  gets AVRCP PASS THROUGH PAUSE (android10 policy); BTA_AvClose /
  BTA_AvOpenRc / BTA_AvCloseRc now use the runtime scb hndl.
- bta_av_aact: NULL scb guard in bta_av_stream_data_cback.

Legacy single-device flow preserved: the first peer's SINK_CFG claims
ownership and posts the same transactional switch; the delayed start
at queue==5 is now race-free.
